        {
            "texttype":"Online",
            "textpurpose":"Description",
            "textentryhtml":"Fire-polished rim; funnel mouth formed into a trefoil; cylindrical neck; sloping shoulder creating a biconical body; splayed, pushed in base. Angular coil handle from shoulder to rim, where there is a projecting tab. Light green thread wound spirally six times around mouth. Another opaque blue thread wound three times around the middle of the body and pinched together at intervals to form loops. At the center of the bottom is a solid, circular pontil mark, 1 cm. wide.",
            "remarks":"Fire and Sand (2012)"
        }
